==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'Behemoth]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*8 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 30~50 seconds<sup>900f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is quite tough, due mostly to the strong Waves and powerful backline. Killing the Two Cans quickly is a must. To achieve this, high DPS units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will be of great help; these units will also stop the Ginger Snaches and Doge Darks from pushing. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is essential too, as it blocks Two Can's Waves and protects your stacks. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] is also helpful if you can quickly kill the Ginger Snaches, ensuring Le'Behemoth doesn't move forward, and at tanking the Two Cans' attacks (though it does make it very easy for them to generate waves). Any unit that outranges Le'Behemoth, like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], or certain Ubers, can deal with it after the Two Cans are disposed of. Bringing [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] is recommended to pierce through its powerful Shield, though be aware that it will easily die if the Two Cans are still alive while it is summoned, as only one Wave will be enough to dispose of it.

